    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Taking extremely high doses of ibuprofen can lead to severe side effects and potentially worsen the burn, rather than help. Second-degree burns often require more extensive treatment than you can manage at home, and not seeking medical attention can cause delayed healing, scarring, and increased risk of infection. It's better to face your fears and seek medical help to get proper assessment and treatment for your burn. Burns can be shallow or deep and spread beneath the skin, without realizing it, so it's crucial to get it evaluated by a medical professional.",
